# Source material for investigation: ISOs, ADFs, real disk images.
# Licensed software and/or large binaries. Never commit.
source-files-do-not-add-to-git/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/
dist/

# Disk images and floppy images: large, and usually licensed software.
#
# These patterns have no slash, so they match at ANY depth -- images/floppy/workbench/3.2/*.adf is
# covered without naming it. The uppercase variants are listed separately and deliberately: git
# matches ignore patterns case-sensitively, and this only appears to work without them because
# core.ignorecase is true on a case-insensitive APFS volume. Amiga media very often arrives
# uppercase (WORKBENCH3.2.ADF), and on a case-sensitive filesystem -- Linux, or a case-sensitive
# APFS volume -- a lowercase-only pattern would let licensed software be committed.
*.hdf
*.HDF
*.hda
*.HDA
*.adf
*.ADF
*.adz
*.ADZ
*.img
*.IMG
*.iso
*.ISO

# Kickstart ROMs. Licensed Cloanto/Amiga material, never committed -- and the split
# `-hi.bin`/`-lo.bin` halves used for flashing real hardware are the same ROM in two pieces,
# so they need covering too. `*.bin` is deliberately NOT ignored globally (too broad, it would
# swallow legitimate test data), so the ROM directory itself is ignored instead.
*.rom
*.ROM
ROMs/
roms/

# User-supplied install media. Never committed: these are licensed Workbench disks, and it is the
# user's job to put their own here. The directory itself is kept so the layout is discoverable.
images/**
!images/**/
!images/**/README.md

# Scratch commit message, written by tooling that cannot use an interactive editor.
.commitmsg

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
